Hi All,

I need help with Subset.
I'm having issues using the Deducer Data Subset tool, and the Deducer wiki entry for Subset is a placeholder only with no information. Basically, I would like to generate a subset of data to exclude entries based on batching two variables per evaluation, I've attached a simple .robj dataset as a simple example.

There are two dataset variables, Sample, and Age that are of importance.

If I do:
====
Sample != ("L1_F1L") & Sample != ("L1_F1R") & Sample != ("L1_F2L")
====
I generate a subset that has samples L1_F1L, L1_F1R and L1_F2L removed.
In my case, this causes issues because there are multiple rows with the same "Sample" string. I only want to exclude those of Age == "E16.5" not "E19.5".

So, I'd like to nest the subset, so it removes Samples L1_F1L, L1_F1R and L1_F2L IF they are 'Age == "E16.5" ' but not if they are "E19.5".

I don't know how to frame the logical expression to evaluate two conditions per row.

best regards,
Kieran

